<title>USA: U.S. primary brass shipments rise in Sept - ABMS.</title>
<headline>U.S. primary brass shipments rise in Sept - ABMS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S primary brass mill shipments rose to 99,700 short tons in September compared to 93,600 tons in August, the American Bureau of Metal Statistics reported.</p>
<p>Brass mill receipts in September were 97,300 tons compared to 87,700 tons in August. Receipts in January to September were 879,000 tons, up from 843,000 tons in the same period last year.</p>
<p>Inventory at brass mills in September totalled 143,000 tons in the form of scrap, refinery shapes and material in progress, compared to 145,500 tons in August.</p>
<p>-- New York Commodities 212-859-1646</p>
</text>
